[1mThe one real mismatch[22m was in exit status, not stdout: when stdout is a pipe with no reader, the C program is killed by [38;5;10mSIGPIPE[0m (status signal 13), but the Rust program exited 0. Rust's runtime sets [38;5;10mSIGPIPE[0m to [38;5;10mSIG_IGN[0m before [38;5;10mmain[0m, so the failing write returned [38;5;10mEPIPE[0m, which the translation discarded. Fixed by calling [38;5;10msignal(SIGPIPE, SIG_DFL)[0m at the top of [38;5;10mmain[0m. I confirmed the test catches it by reverting the fix — it fails with [38;5;10mleft: signal 13 / right: exit 0[0m — then restored it.[0m[0m
