- [38;5;10ms[strlen(s)-1] = '\0'[0m is unconditional, so on a line truncated at fgets' 99-byte limit or ending at EOF without a newline it strips a [3mdata[23m byte, not a newline. A 99-byte line also leaves the rest of the physical line for the second [38;5;10mfgets[0m, so [38;5;10ms2[0m can come from the same input line as [38;5;10ms1[0m.[0m[0m
